# everything that decides what gets signed, or that holds a secret boundary,
# needs the owner on the pull request. a skill folder does not: the release
# statement inside it is signed by its own publisher's key and the build job
# refuses anything that is not.
# the generated marketplace file decides, for every plugin name, whose
# folder a `claude plugin install` copies. that is the same question the
# signing boundary answers, one layer out, so it gets the same review.
.claude-plugin/** @Adoom666
.github/**      @Adoom666
tools/**        @Adoom666
publishers/**   @Adoom666
# a committed review is published verbatim into the signed index, so it is
# text this repository vouches for.
reviews/**      @Adoom666
catalog.yml     @Adoom666
CODEOWNERS      @Adoom666
